IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fa-families`

-- A New Tax System (Family Assistance) Act 1999 (Cth) -- FTB Part A with rent assistance and the maintenance income test, and the
-- Schedule 4 indexation of the rates, computed from the formulas recovered on 2026-10-24, beside fa-families.l4 (unchanged).
--
-- fa-families.l4 leaves out rent assistance (Sch 1 cl 3 step 1(d)) and takes maintenance income as nil (cl 3 step 3), because the
-- formulas of Sch 1 cll 20A, 38D and 38E were lost from the text deposit. The sidecar
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00490.formulas.md ("Further entries, recovered 2026-10-24") now gives them:
--   * cl 38D (Method 1, at least one FTB child, not a relevant shared carer): Rate A = ((Annual rent - threshold) / 4) x 3, the
--     threshold $5,000.50 (not a member of a couple, and the gaol, illness, respite and temporarily separated couples) or
--     $7,391.25 (other members of a couple), "but only up to" Rate B ($6,343.70 for 1 or 2 rent assistance children, $7,168.60 for
--     3 or more);
--   * cl 20A(2): annualised maintenance = maintenance received in the relevant period x (days in the income year / days in the
--     relevant period);
--   * Sch 4 cl 5(1): indexation factor = index number for most recent reference quarter / index number for base quarter.
-- The rest is text: cl 38C (eligibility), cl 20 (the reduction is half the excess over the maintenance income free area), cl 21
-- (a couple's annualised amounts added), cl 22 (the free area), cl 19B (blind pensioners), Sch 4 cll 4, 5(2), (3), 6.
--
-- SCOPE of the maintenance income test: maintenance from ONE payer for ALL the FTB children, with no regular care child who is a
-- rent assistance child. Then cll 24F and 24M say Subdivisions C and D (the maintenance income ceilings, cll 24G-24S, whose
-- formulas are also in the sidecar) do not apply, so no ceiling is needed. Any other arrangement answers `not covered`.
-- Rent assistance is the cl 38D table only (no relevant shared carer, no regular care child: cl 38E is not encoded).
-- The dollar figures are indexed (Sch 4 cl 2 items 4, 4A, 12, 15, 16): they are inputs, in `Rent and maintenance figures`, with
-- the printed set as a labelled example. The CPI index numbers are inputs.
--
-- SEAT: the parent, as in fa-families.l4. Edition: Compilation No. 124 (C2026C00331). BASELINE. See NOTES.md.

§ `Family Assistance Act -- amounts computed from the recovered formulas`

§§ `Sch 1 cll 38B-38F -- rent assistance (Method 1)`

DECLARE `Rent and maintenance figures` HAS
    `rent threshold, single or separated couple`        IS A NUMBER  -- cl 38C(1)(f)(i), (iii), (iv); cl 38D items 1, 3, 4
    `rent threshold, member of a couple`                IS A NUMBER  -- cl 38C(1)(f)(ii); cl 38D item 2
    `maximum rent assistance, 1 or 2 children`          IS A NUMBER  -- cl 38D column 3A (Rate B)
    `maximum rent assistance, 3 or more children`       IS A NUMBER  -- cl 38D column 3B (Rate B)
    `maintenance income free area, basic amount`        IS A NUMBER  -- cl 22 items 1 and 3, column 2
    `maintenance income free area, basic amount, both partners receive maintenance` IS A NUMBER  -- cl 22 item 2, column 2
    `maintenance income free area, additional amount`   IS A NUMBER  -- cl 22 column 3

-- The figures as printed in Compilation No. 124. Indexed (Sch 4 cl 2): not the figures paid in any given year.
`the rent and maintenance figures as printed in Compilation No. 124` MEANS `Rent and maintenance figures` WITH
    `rent threshold, single or separated couple`        IS 5000.50
    `rent threshold, member of a couple`                IS 7391.25
    `maximum rent assistance, 1 or 2 children`          IS 6343.70
    `maximum rent assistance, 3 or more children`       IS 7168.60
    `maintenance income free area, basic amount`        IS 952.65
    `maintenance income free area, basic amount, both partners receive maintenance` IS 1905.30
    `maintenance income free area, additional amount`   IS 317.55

DECLARE `My rent and maintenance` HAS
    `my couple is separated by gaol, illness or respite care, or temporarily` IS A BOOLEAN  -- cl 38D items 3, 4
    `my rent assistance children`                       IS A NUMBER   -- cl 38B(2): FTB children whose child rate exceeds the base rate
    `I pay rent other than Government rent`             IS A BOOLEAN  -- cl 38C(1)(e)
    `my annual rent`                                    IS A NUMBER   -- cl 38F, with my partner's (cll 38G, 38H)
    `I am an ineligible homeowner or an aged care resident` IS A BOOLEAN  -- cl 38C(1)(c), (d)
    `my claim is for a past period without an instalment claim, or I or my partner get incentive allowance` IS A BOOLEAN  -- cl 38C(1)(b), (ba), (2)
    `I am a relevant shared carer`                      IS A BOOLEAN  -- cl 38E (not encoded)
    `maintenance received in the relevant period`       IS A NUMBER   -- cl 20A(2), with my partner's (cl 21); 0 if none
    `days in the income year`                           IS A NUMBER   -- cl 20A(2)
    `days in the relevant period`                       IS A NUMBER   -- cl 20A(3)-(9)
    `my partner and I both receive maintenance`         IS A BOOLEAN  -- cl 22 item 2
    `the maintenance is from one payer for all my FTB children` IS A BOOLEAN  -- cll 24F, 24M
    `I or my partner am permanently blind and receive an age or disability support pension or the like` IS A BOOLEAN  -- cl 19B

DECLARE `Amount or not covered` IS ONE OF
    `an amount` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `not covered`

-- cl 38C(1): rent assistance is added if "(a) the individual has at least one rent assistance child", the claim is not a (2) claim,
-- no incentive allowance, "(c) the individual is not an ineligible homeowner; and (d) ... not an aged care resident; and (e) the
-- individual pays, or is liable to pay, rent (other than Government rent); and (f) if the individual has at least one FTB child
-- and is not a relevant shared carer -- the rent is payable at a rate of more than" the threshold for the family situation.
-- cl 38D: Rate A by the formula, "but only up to the individual's maximum rent assistance rate", Rate B.
@export How much rent assistance is added to my maximum rate of FTB Part A a year (Sch 1 cll 38B-38F)?
GIVEN `figures` IS A `Rent and maintenance figures` @desc The rent thresholds and maximum rent assistance rates in force
      `f` IS A `My family` @desc Your family
      `r` IS A `My rent and maintenance` @desc Your rent, and the rent assistance facts
GIVETH AN `Amount or not covered`
`How much rent assistance do I get a year` MEANS
    IF `r`'s `I am a relevant shared carer`
    THEN `not covered`
    ELSE IF     `the number of FTB children` `f` AT LEAST 1
            AND `r`'s `my rent assistance children` AT LEAST 1
            AND `r`'s `I pay rent other than Government rent`
            AND NOT `r`'s `I am an ineligible homeowner or an aged care resident`
            AND NOT `r`'s `my claim is for a past period without an instalment claim, or I or my partner get incentive allowance`
            AND `r`'s `my annual rent` GREATER THAN `threshold`
         THEN `an amount` (min `Rate B` (((`r`'s `my annual rent` MINUS `threshold`) DIVIDED BY 4) TIMES 3))
         ELSE `an amount` 0
    WHERE
        `threshold` MEANS
            IF `f`'s `I am a member of a couple` AND NOT `r`'s `my couple is separated by gaol, illness or respite care, or temporarily`
            THEN `figures`'s `rent threshold, member of a couple`
            ELSE `figures`'s `rent threshold, single or separated couple`
        `Rate B` MEANS
            IF `r`'s `my rent assistance children` AT LEAST 3
            THEN `figures`'s `maximum rent assistance, 3 or more children`
            ELSE `figures`'s `maximum rent assistance, 1 or 2 children`

§§ `Sch 1 cll 19B-23 -- the maintenance income test (one payer for all the children)`

-- cl 20A(2), formula (sidecar): The amount of maintenance income (other than CMI) received by the individual during the relevant
-- period or periods x (Number of days in the income year / Number of days in the relevant period or periods). cl 21: a couple's
-- annualised amounts are added (the input is the couple's total).
@export What is the annualised amount of my maintenance income (Sch 1 cll 20A(2), 21)?
GIVEN `r` IS A `My rent and maintenance` @desc The maintenance you (and your partner) received, and over how many days
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my annualised maintenance income` MEANS
    IF `r`'s `days in the relevant period` AT MOST 0 THEN 0
    ELSE `r`'s `maintenance received in the relevant period` TIMES (`r`'s `days in the income year` DIVIDED BY `r`'s `days in the relevant period`)

-- cl 22: "the corresponding amount in column 2 plus an additional corresponding amount in column 3 for each FTB child after the
-- first": item 1 not a member of a couple, item 2 partnered with both receiving maintenance, item 3 partnered with one.
@export What is my maintenance income free area (Sch 1 cl 22)?
GIVEN `figures` IS A `Rent and maintenance figures` @desc The free area amounts in force
      `f` IS A `My family` @desc Your family
      `r` IS A `My rent and maintenance` @desc Whether you and your partner both receive maintenance
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my maintenance income free area` MEANS
    `basic` PLUS (`figures`'s `maintenance income free area, additional amount` TIMES `the positive part of` (`the number of FTB children` `f` MINUS 1))
    WHERE
        `basic` MEANS
            IF `f`'s `I am a member of a couple` AND `r`'s `my partner and I both receive maintenance`
            THEN `figures`'s `maintenance income free area, basic amount, both partners receive maintenance`
            ELSE `figures`'s `maintenance income free area, basic amount`

-- cl 20(1) Steps 3-6: "The individual's reduction for maintenance income is half the maintenance income excess" over the free
-- area. cl 19B: nil for a blind age or disability support pensioner couple. Outside one payer for all the children, the
-- ceilings of Subdivisions C and D apply: not covered.
@export What is my reduction for maintenance income a year (Sch 1 cll 19B, 20)?
GIVEN `figures` IS A `Rent and maintenance figures` @desc The free area amounts in force
      `f` IS A `My family` @desc Your family
      `r` IS A `My rent and maintenance` @desc Your maintenance
GIVETH AN `Amount or not covered`
`What is my reduction for maintenance income` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `r`'s `maintenance received in the relevant period` AT MOST 0 THEN `an amount` 0
           IF `r`'s `I or my partner am permanently blind and receive an age or disability support pension or the like` THEN `an amount` 0
           IF NOT `r`'s `the maintenance is from one payer for all my FTB children` THEN `not covered`
           OTHERWISE `an amount` (`the positive part of` (`What is my annualised maintenance income` `r` MINUS `What is my maintenance income free area` `figures` `f` `r`) DIVIDED BY 2)

§§ `Sch 1 cll 3, 25, 25D -- FTB Part A with rent assistance and maintenance`

-- cl 3 Step 1(d) adds rent assistance to the maximum rate; Step 3 takes the maintenance reduction from the income tested rate;
-- Step 4: the base rate if higher. cl 25 Step 3 with cl 25D: the Method 2 income and maintenance tested rate is the Method 1
-- maximum rate (so with rent assistance) less 20% of (HIFA - IFA), 30% of (income - HIFA) and the maintenance reduction; Step 4:
-- the greater of that and the provisional Part A rate. The same arithmetic as fa-families.l4's `How much FTB Part A do I get a
-- year`, with the two additions; with no rent and no maintenance it gives the same answer.
@desc FTB Part A a year with a given rent assistance amount and maintenance reduction added to the Method 1 and Method 2 arithmetic
GIVEN `the rates` IS A Rates @desc The indexed rates in force
      `f` IS A `My family` @desc Your family
      `ra` IS A NUMBER @desc Rent assistance a year
      `mit` IS A NUMBER @desc Reduction for maintenance income a year
GIVETH A NUMBER
`FTB Part A with rent assistance and a maintenance reduction` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the number of FTB children` `f` EQUALS 0 THEN 0
           IF `Is my FTB Part A worked out by Method 1` `the rates` `f`
           THEN max (`income tested rate before rent assistance` PLUS `ra` MINUS `mit`) `base rate`
           OTHERWISE `the positive part of` (max `provisional Part A rate` `Method 2 income and maintenance tested rate`)
    WHERE
        `income`       MEANS `What income is my FTB Part A tested on` `f`
        `maximum rate` MEANS `What is my maximum rate of FTB Part A` `the rates` `f`
        `base rate`    MEANS `What is my base rate of FTB Part A` `the rates` `f`
        `HIFA`         MEANS `the rates`'s `higher income free area`
        `IFA`          MEANS `the rates`'s `income free area (A)`
        `income tested rate before rent assistance` MEANS
            IF `f`'s `I or my partner get a pension or benefit`
            THEN `maximum rate`
            ELSE `maximum rate` MINUS `percent of` 20 (`the positive part of` (`income` MINUS `IFA`))
        `provisional Part A rate` MEANS `base rate` MINUS `percent of` 30 (`income` MINUS `HIFA`)
        `Method 2 income and maintenance tested rate` MEANS
            ((`maximum rate` PLUS `ra`) MINUS `percent of` 20 (`HIFA` MINUS `IFA`)) MINUS (`percent of` 30 (`income` MINUS `HIFA`) PLUS `mit`)

@export How much FTB Part A do I get a year, with rent assistance and the maintenance income test (Sch 1 cll 3, 20, 25, 38D)?
GIVEN `the rates` IS A Rates @desc The indexed rates in force
      `figures` IS A `Rent and maintenance figures` @desc The rent assistance and maintenance figures in force
      `f` IS A `My family` @desc Your family
      `r` IS A `My rent and maintenance` @desc Your rent and maintenance
GIVETH AN `Amount or not covered`
`How much FTB Part A do I get a year with rent and maintenance` MEANS
    CONSIDER `How much rent assistance do I get a year` `figures` `f` `r`
    WHEN `not covered` THEN `not covered`
    WHEN `an amount` `ra` THEN
        CONSIDER `What is my reduction for maintenance income` `figures` `f` `r`
        WHEN `not covered` THEN `not covered`
        WHEN `an amount` `mit` THEN `an amount` (`FTB Part A with rent assistance and a maintenance reduction` `the rates` `f` `ra` `mit`)

§§ `Sch 4 cll 4-6 -- indexation of the rates`

-- Sch 4 cl 5(1), formula (sidecar): Index number for most recent reference quarter / Index number for base quarter, "worked out to
-- 3 decimal places"; (2) raised by 0.001 if the 4th decimal place "is greater than 4"; (3) never below 1. cl 4(2): the current
-- figure times the factor, rounded under cl 6 to the nearest multiple of the rounding base, a half rounded up. The rounding base is
-- column 5 of the cl 3 CPI Indexation Table for the amount. The CPI index numbers are INPUTS. Clauses 10 and 11 (pauses) are not
-- modelled.
@export What is the Schedule 4 indexation factor (Sch 4 cl 5)?
GIVEN `index number for most recent reference quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The CPI index number for the reference quarter
      `index number for base quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The CPI index number for the base quarter
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the FTB indexation factor` MEANS
    IF `raised` LESS THAN 1 THEN 1 ELSE `raised`
    WHERE
        `ratio` MEANS `index number for most recent reference quarter` DIVIDED BY `index number for base quarter`
        `to 3 places` MEANS FLOOR (`ratio` TIMES 1000) DIVIDED BY 1000
        `fourth place` MEANS FLOOR (`ratio` TIMES 10000) MINUS (FLOOR (`ratio` TIMES 1000) TIMES 10)
        `raised` MEANS IF `fourth place` GREATER THAN 4 THEN `to 3 places` PLUS 0.001 ELSE `to 3 places`

@export What is an amount after a Schedule 4 indexation (Sch 4 cll 4, 6)?
GIVEN `current figure` IS A NUMBER @desc The current figure for the amount immediately before the indexation day
      `index number for most recent reference quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The CPI index number for the reference quarter
      `index number for base quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The CPI index number for the base quarter
      `rounding base` IS A NUMBER @desc Column 5 of the Sch 4 cl 3 table for the amount
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the FTB indexed amount` MEANS
    FLOOR ((`current figure` TIMES `What is the FTB indexation factor` `index number for most recent reference quarter` `index number for base quarter`
            DIVIDED BY `rounding base`) PLUS 0.5)
    TIMES `rounding base`
